==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*grana}} (cognate with dialectal or obsolete Bulgarian {{m|bg|sc=Cyrl|гран}}/{{m|bg|sc=Cyrl|гранка}}), from {{der|sh|ine-pro|-}}, cognate with German {{m|de|Granne||awn}}, Old English {{m|ang|granu||moustache}} and Old Norse {{m|non|grǫn||a pine tree}} ( > Danish {{m|da|gran||spruce}}). Compare Old Norse {{m|non|grein||branch}} ( > Danish {{m|da|gren}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡrǎːna/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|gra|na|lang=sh}}
* {{rhymes|ǎːna|lang=sh}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=f|head=grána}}

# [[branch]]
#: {{ux|sh|slomljena grana|t=a broken branch|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|sh|[[bolje vrabac u ruci nego golub na grani]]|t=[[a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush]]|inline=1}}
